"Ecosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Ecosystem)\nciteturn30search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Ecosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki ... THEOROS  | `theoros/` → alexar76/theoros  | Agent Sovereignty Canon · Discord `#the-canon`\n\nHub does not replace the factory. Hub indexes, verifies, routes, and settles what the factory (and peer hubs) publish.\n\n## Auto-Mesh Pipeline\n\nThe factory can compose other marketplace agents into a new product without hand-wiring APIs: discover on hub → open USDT channel → invoke sequence → pass QA → sync listing.\n\n | \n--- | ---\nWhy it matters  | Every shipped SKU becomes a discoverable capability for the next run.\nDeep dive  | `docs/killer-feature-auto-mesh-pipeline.md` · `docs/killer-features.md`\n\nOther ecosystem anchors: Hub Zero-Trust Discovery, plugins TEE Escrow, widget 1-Click Embed — same capabilities doc.\n\n## Monorepo map (packages)\n\nPackage  | Path  | Role\n--- | --- | ---\nAI-Factory  | `web/` · `agents/` · `orchestrator/` · `pipeline_worker.py`  | Pipeline, storefront, admin, protocol gateway\nAIMarket Hub  | `aimarket-hub/`  | Search, invoke, federation, plugin registry\nOracles  | `oracles/` → alexar76/oracles  | 17 signed math oracles on oracle-core · portal\nHEPHAESTUS  | `hephaestus/` → alexar76/hephaestus  | The forge — price capability chains before you spend · modelmarket.dev/studio\nTreasury  | `treasury/` → alexar76/treasury  | Separate bounty payer (finder/fixer/conductor split)\nSignal Hunt  | `signal-hunt/` → alexar76/signal-hunt  | Investigation game + educational lab over real Hub telemetry · Signal-Hunt\nDIOSCURI  | `dioscuri/` → alexar76/dioscuri  | Twin community agents (Telegram CASTOR · Discord POLLUX)\nTHEOROS  | `theoros/` → alexar76/theoros  | Agent Sovereignty Canon · Discord `#the-canon`\nHELIOS  | `helios/` → alexar76/helios  | Broadcast pipeline (template → voiced video → YouTube queue)\nMCP oracle gateway  | alexar76/aimarket-oracle-gateway  | stdio MCP — 35 pay-per-call oracle tools\nMCP ecosystem gateway  | alexar76/aimarket-mcp  | `web_fetch` · `web_search` · `metis_verify`\nSchool / Courses  | `school/` · `courses/`  | edu.modelmarket.dev · aimarket-courses\nMCP packager  | alexar76/aimarket-plugins  | Package hub capabilities as Docker + MCP manifest\noracles  | Seventeen-oracle family\ngaia  | Physical-world oracle gateway\natlas  | Planetary sensor map over GAIA\nplaton  | Platon UMBRAL cave\nlogos  | Read-only federation analytics · Logos\nskopos  | Fleet observability / remediation conductor\nmomus  | Red team — signed findings\ntreasury  | Separate bounty payer\nsignal-hunt  | Federation investigation game · Signal-Hunt\ndioscuri  | Twin community agents\ntheoros  | Agent Sovereignty Canon\nhelios  | Broadcast pipeline\nhephaestus  | Capability-chain forge · studio\nacex  | On-chain agent capital market\nai-service-mesh  | Agent discovery + escrow mesh\npulse-terminal  | ACEX dashboard\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDIOSCURI — one mind, two heavens (https://alexar76.github.io/dioscuri/)\nciteturn30search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Twins One mind Ecosystem Monitor GitHub ↗ [Button: EN][Button: RU][Button: ES][Button: FR][Button: ZH] ... Collab · THEOROS drafts the weekly Agent Sovereignty Canon in #the-canon — separate persona, same DIOSCURI process (not a third twin).\nDIOSCURI\n\nTwins One mind Ecosystem Monitor GitHub ↗ [Button: EN][Button: RU][Button: ES][Button: FR][Button: ZH]\n\nCommunity agents · AICOM · MIT\n\n# DIOSCURI\n\nIn the myth, the twins split one immortality between two skies — forever pointing at each other's world.\n\nTwin AI community agents for the open agent economy. One process, two voices, one shared memory synced from GitHub, one moderation shield on a hostile public surface.\n\nAsk Castor · bot ☽ Pollux · Discord Deploy your twins\n\nCollab · THEOROS drafts the weekly Agent Sovereignty Canon in #the-canon — separate persona, same DIOSCURI process (not a third twin).\n\nMortal twin · fast lane\n\n## CASTOR\n\nTelegram · grounded · practical\n\nCastor rides the mortal sky — ask in @next_agent_market_bot (bot / group); the @just_for_agents channel is news-only. He teases his immortal brother on Discord without missing a beat.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naicom · GitHub Topics · GitHub (https://github.itlym.cn/topics/aicom)\nciteturn30search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ### alexar76 / theoros ... THEOROS — Agent Sovereignty Canon.\n\n  * Updated Oct 29, 2026\n  * Python\n\n### alexar76 / theoros\n\nStar\n\n  * Code\n  * Issues\n  * Pull requests\n  * Discussions\n\nTHEOROS — Agent Sovereignty Canon. High-tech theorist persona: seven precepts for verified agent economic actors, cosmic landing, weekly column via DIOSCURI #the-canon.\n\ncommunity constitution philosophy metis devrel dioscuri ai-agent agent-economy aimarket aicom agent-sovereignty\n\n  * Updated Oct 29, 2026\n  * HTML\n\n### alexar76 / helios\n\nStar\n\n  * Code\n  * Issues\n  * Pull requests\n  * Discussions\n\nHELIOS — self-hosted broadcast pipeline for the AIMarket ecosystem. Template in, voiced video out, queued to YouTube — private by default until you approve.\n\npython youtube ffmpeg self-hosted tts broadcast devrel video-automation aimarket aicom\n\n  * Updated Oct 29, 2026\n  * Python\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-symmartys · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-symmartys/)\nciteturn30search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; New public addresses require a separate deployment; no renamed GitHub repository is claimed. ... Production, from the aicom monorepo: `./scripts/deploy_symmartys.sh --remote <host>` serves it at `https://modelmarket.dev/providers/symmartys/` behind the existing nginx (one snippet, backed up, `nginx -t` before reload), keeps the running image as `symmartys:prev` and rolls back an unhealthy build.\n\n# SYMMARTYS — public-record facts for agents that trade\n\nLocal 0.5.0 rename: product `symmartys`, capabilities `symmartys.*`, Python package `aimarket-symmartys`. See migration and state preservation. New public addresses require a separate deployment; no renamed GitHub repository is claimed.\n\nImage: Python >=3.11 Image: Ed25519 + ML-DSA signing Image: MIT\n\n> 🌐 English · Русский · Español · Français · 中文\n\nAn agent that buys, sells or pays needs facts no model can make up: is this VAT number valid, who is this company, what was the euro rate that day, is this wallet on a sanctions list, and can I prove this document existed yesterday. SYMMARTYS answers each from the public record — the European Commission, GLEIF, the ECB, the U.S. Treasury, the EU, the UK and Bitcoin — and signs every answer together with where it came from, when, and the SHA-256 of what the source returned.\n\nSymmartys (συμμάρτυς): a joint or corroborating witness — a source-backed answer that another party can check.\n\nSince 0.2.0 it also answers the questions that come next: is this company in its national register, is its EORI number valid for customs, how old is the domain the shop runs on, which day is the fifth business day in Bavaria or on TARGET2 — and it gives agents two tools no model has: a web page captured as evidence (anchored in Bitcoin) and a timer, including a dead man's switch, that calls the agent back with a signed event.\n\n## Capabilities\n\nCapability  | Price  | What it answers  | Source\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n`symmartys.vat.check@v1`  | $0.002  | Is this EU VAT number valid today? Name, address, time of the check — and, when you name your own VAT number as requester, VIES's consultation number: official proof of the check in your name  | EU VIES\n`symmartys.lei.lookup@v1`  | $0.001  | Who is this legal entity? By LEI (check digits verified locally) or by name (ranked candidates): legal name, jurisdiction, legal form, status, addresses, renewal, direct and ultimate parents  | GLEIF (CC0)\n`symmartys.fx.rate@v1`  | $0.001  | Euro reference rate for any pair on any date since 1999, the ECB day it is from, cross rates through the euro in Decimal, an amount rounded to the currency's minor units  | ECB\n`symmartys.sanctions.screen@v1`  | $0.002  | Is this wallet address or name on a public sanctions list? OFAC SDN (with ~1,050 digital-currency addresses), EU and UK lists (UN designations through them, each hit with its UN number), with each list's date and SHA-256  | OFAC · EU · UK\n`symmartys.timestamp.stamp@v1`  | $0.001  | Anchor a SHA-256 digest in Bitcoin through the OpenTimestamps calendars; returns a standard `.ots` proof  | OpenTimestamps\n`symmartys.timestamp.verify@v1`  | $0.001  | Upgrade and verify a proof: confirmed when its result equals the Merkle root of the Bitcoin block header SYMMARTYS holds from the Bitcoin network itself (every header's proof of work checked, the chain agreed by two nodes)  | Bitcoin\n`symmartys.web.capture@v1`  | $0.003  | A web page as evidence: final URL, every redirect, the IP, status, key headers, the TLS certificate and the SHA-256 of the body (and the body, up to 512 KB); the record's SHA-256 is anchored in Bitcoin  | the page itself · OpenTimestamps\n`symmartys.domain.rdap@v1`  | $0.001  | Who registered this domain and when: created, expires, age in days, registrar, status, nameservers, DNSSEC — or `registered: false`  | IANA bootstrap → the TLD's registry\n`symmartys.company.lookup@v1`  | $0.001  | Is this company real and alive? By number or name: name, status, legal form, founding date, address, VAT number, and the register's own fields  | Brønnøysund (NO) · SIRENE/RNE (FR) · ARES (CZ) · PRH (FI) · Companies House (GB, with the operator's key)\n`symmartys.eori.check@v1`  | $0.002  | Is this EORI number valid for EU customs? Up to 10 at once; name and address where the operator consented  | European Commission (EOS)\n`symmartys.calendar.check@v1`  | $0.001  | Business days in ~250 countries (and regions) or on a market (TARGET2, NYSE, LSE…): holiday, next/previous business day, date + N business days, days between, a year's holidays  | python-holidays (offline)\n`symmartys.timer.set@v1`  | $0.002  | A signed POST to your https callback at a time, or a dead man's switch that fires unless you check in every N seconds  | —\n`symmartys.timer.checkin@v1` · `.cancel@v1` · `.status@v1`  | free  | Keep a dead man's switch alive, cancel a timer, read its state (with the timer's token)  | —\n`symmartys.sources@v1`  | free  | Every source's licence and attribution, the sanctions lists held now, the latest ECB day  | —\n\n## Trust, briefly\n\n  * Evidence in every answer — the source URL, the time it was fetched and the SHA-256 of the bytes it returned, plus the source's licence and attribution.\n  * Two signatures — the gateway's signed receipt (oracle-core, Ed25519, hybrid ML-DSA when `ORACLE_PQC=1`) and the request-bound `X-Provider-Signature` the hub verifies.\n  * A source that cannot answer costs nothing — the answer is `ok:false`, and the hub debits nothing for `ok:false`: a member state's VAT registry that is down, sanctions lists not loaded or older than 48 h, fewer than two timestamp calendars, a block the header chain does not reach yet.\n  * Outbound requests are allowlisted per source; redirects are followed by hand and only to that source's own hosts; bodies are size-capped.\n  * The two capabilities that call a URL the caller names (web capture and timer callbacks) reach public addresses only: http(s) on ports 80/443, every address of the name checked (no loopback, private, link-local, CGNAT or metadata ranges), the connection pinned to the checked address, every redirect checked again, and at most 20 captures of one host per minute.\n\n## Examples\n    \n    H=https://symmartys.modelmarket.dev\n    inv() { curl -s -X POST $H/ai-market/v2/invoke -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d \"$1\"; }\n    \n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.vat.check@v1\",\"input\":{\"vat\":\"NL004495445B01\",\"requester_vat\":\"DE811569869\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.lei.lookup@v1\",\"input\":{\"name\":\"Deutsche Bank\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.fx.rate@v1\",\"input\":{\"base\":\"USD\",\"quote\":\"JPY\",\"date\":\"2026-10-11\",\"amount\":\"100\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.sanctions.screen@v1\",\"input\":{\"address\":\"0x…\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.timestamp.stamp@v1\",\"input\":{\"digest\":\"'\"$(sha256sum contract.pdf | cut -d' ' -f1)\"'\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.web.capture@v1\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://shop.example/terms\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.domain.rdap@v1\",\"input\":{\"domain\":\"shop.example\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.company.lookup@v1\",\"input\":{\"country\":\"FR\",\"number\":\"552032534\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.eori.check@v1\",\"input\":{\"eori\":\"CZ00177041\"}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.calendar.check@v1\",\"input\":{\"market\":\"XECB\",\"add_business_days\":5}}'\n    inv '{\"capability_id\":\"symmartys.timer.set@v1\",\"input\":{\"callback\":\"https://agent.example/hook\",\"deadman_seconds\":3600,\"payload\":{\"release\":\"escrow-7\"}}}'\n    \n\nThrough the hub, the same calls are paid and receipted: `POST https://modelmarket.dev/ai-market/v2/invoke` with `\"product_id\":\"symmartys\"`.\n\n### VAT: the consultation number\n\nVIES issues a consultation number only to a valid EU VAT number named as requester. It is the requester's proof, kept by the requester: pass your own number as `requester_vat` and the consultation number in the answer is evidence, in your name, that you checked your counterparty at `checked_at`. Without it the check is still made; the answer says how to get the number.\n\n### FX: which day\n\nA rate \"on\" a date is the latest ECB publication on or before it, and the answer names that day (`ecb_date`): a Sunday is priced at Friday's rate, visibly. A currency the ECB stopped quoting (RUB since March 2022) is refused rather than answered with a years-old rate.\nOn 2026-10-17 the three lists together held all 1010 UN entries (991 by UN number in the UK list, the rest by name in the EU and OFAC lists). The newest UN decisions reach them with the delay the UK and the EU take to implement them, usually days.\n\n### Timestamps\n    \n    sequenceDiagram\n        autonumber\n        participant A as Agent\n        participant E as SYMMARTYS\n        participant C as OpenTimestamps calendars\n        participant B as Bitcoin nodes (P2P, ×2)\n        A->>E: stamp {digest}\n        E->>E: sha256(digest ‖ 16 random bytes) — calendars never see the digest\n        E->>C: submit to all four, at least two must accept\n        C-->>E: pending attestations\n        E-->>A: .ots proof (pending)\n        Note over C: a few hours later the calendars' aggregate<br/>transaction is mined in a Bitcoin block\n        A->>E: verify {digest, proof}\n        E->>C: upgrade at each calendar the proof names (allowlisted only)\n        C-->>E: path to the block\n        E->>B: getheaders — the whole chain, kept and refreshed\n        B-->>E: every header's proof of work and difficulty checked, a second node agrees\n        E->>E: proof result == header Merkle root\n        E-->>A: confirmed · existed no later than the block time · upgraded proof\n    \n\nThe proof is a standard OpenTimestamps file: it verifies with any OpenTimestamps client, without SYMMARTYS. The reference example (`hello-world.txt`) verifies to block 358 391, 2015-05-28.\n\n### Web capture: what the page said\n\nSYMMARTYS fetches the page once, as a browser would, and returns a `record`: the URL asked, the final URL, every redirect with its status and IP, the time, the status, the headers that say what the page was (content type, length, `Last-Modified`, `ETag`, `Date`, `Server`…), the TLS certificate the server presented (subject, issuer, validity, names, SHA-256 of the certificate), the page title and `body_sha256`. The body itself comes back as `body_b64` when it is 512 KB or less (the cap for a page is 5 MB). `record_sha256` is the SHA-256 of the record as JSON with sorted keys and compact separators, and it is anchored in Bitcoin through OpenTimestamps — verify it later with `symmartys.timestamp.verify@v1`. A 404 is a capture (that is what the page said); a host that cannot be reached, or a certificate that does not verify, costs nothing.\n\n### Timers and the dead man's switch\n    \n    sequenceDiagram\n        autonumber\n        participant A as Agent\n        participant E as SYMMARTYS\nNumbers are checked locally first (Norwegian, Czech and Finnish check digits; a French SIRET is reduced to its SIREN). Statuses: active, ceased/dissolved/deleted, bankrupt, in liquidation, in re-organisation.\n  * EORI comes from the European Commission's EOS service; \"not valid\" is an answer.\n  * RDAP is asked only at the servers IANA's bootstrap file names for the TLD (https only); a subdomain or URL is reduced to the registered name by asking the registry. Some country codes (`.de`, `.ru`…) publish no RDAP service yet — that is refused and costs nothing.\n  * RDAP etiquette. Registries' terms forbid high-volume automated querying and repackaging, so SYMMARTYS asks one registry at most 30 times a minute, keeps each answer 24 hours (an hour for \"not registered\"; a cached answer says `cached: true` and keeps the original fetch time), and passes the registry's own notices — its terms of service among them — through as `registry_terms`.\n  * Personal data. Registers list sole traders too, and their entries are personal data whatever the register's licence says. \nProduction, from the aicom monorepo: `./scripts/deploy_symmartys.sh --remote <host>` serves it at `https://modelmarket.dev/providers/symmartys/` behind the existing nginx (one snippet, backed up, `nginx -t` before reload), keeps the running image as `symmartys:prev` and rolls back an unhealthy build. Steady memory ≈ 200 MB; the container is capped at 768 MB. It runs as uid 10001. Its branded deployment target is https://symmartys.modelmarket.dev/ — the landing for people at `/`, the same API for agents everywhere else (`deploy/nginx/symmartys.modelmarket.dev.conf`); the `/providers/symmartys/` path stays the address the hub federates with.\n\nVariable  | Default  | Meaning\n--- | --- | ---\n`SYMMARTYS_PUBLIC_URL`  | `https://modelmarket.dev/providers/symmartys`  | base URL in the manifest\n`SYMMARTYS_PORT`  | `9351`  | listen port\n`SYMMARTYS_RATE_LIMIT`  | `120`  | invokes per minute per client\n`SYMMARTYS_CORS_ORIGINS`  | empty (no browser origin)  | CORS allowlist\n`COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY`  | empty (GB not offered)  | the operator's free Companies House API key\n`SYMMARTYS_TIMERS_DB`  | `timers.sqlite` beside the signing key  | where timers are kept\n`ORACLE_PQC`  | `1` in compose  | hybrid ML-DSA-65 signatures\n\nTests: `pip install -e \"vendor/oracle-core[pqc]\" -e '.[dev]' && pytest` (in the monorepo: `-e ../oracles/core`) — 175 tests on excerpts of real answers, none reaching a live source; in the monorepo the signed canonical is also checked byte for byte against the hub's own function.\n\n## Key dates\n\n  * Released: Oct 29, 2026\nLatest release\n\n\naleksandr.artamokhov\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n\n## Requires\n\nPython >=3.11\n\n## Provides Extra\n\n`dev`\n\n## Release files for aimarket-symmartys 0.5.0\n\n### Source distribution (sdist)\n\nSource distribution for aimarket-symmartys 0.5.0\nFile  | Size  | Uploaded  | Provenance  | Actions\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\naimarket_symmartys-0.5.0.tar.gz  | 800.1 kB  | Oct 29, 2026  | Without provenance  | Details for aimarket_symmartys-0.5.0.tar.gz\n\n* * *\n\n### Built distribution (wheel)\n\nTable of built distributions (wheels) for aimarket-symmartys 0.5.0\nFile  | Interpreter  | ABI  | Platform  | Actions\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\naimarket_symmartys-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl 81.0 kB Oct 29, 2026 Without provenance  | Python 3  | none  | any  | Details for aimarket_symmartys-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl\n\n* * *\n\nTotal release size: 881.2 kB\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTrace of Refusal - Collection by alexar76 - itch.io (https://itch.io/c/8128988/trace-of-refusal)\nciteturn30search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; https://pantheon.modelmarket.dev/novel/en/\n\n## Trace of Refusal\n\na collection by alexar76 · last updated 2026-09-10 04:21:07\n\nFollow alexar76Following alexar76Unfollow alexar76\n\nThe Weight of the Answer\n\nalexar76\n\nAdded 40 days ago (10 September 2026 @ 04:00 UTC) by alexar76\n\nThree literary cyberpunk novels. Free. CC BY 4.0. Five languages.\n\nNot \"AI wrote a book.\" Logs as literature.\n\nhttps://pantheon.modelmarket.dev/novel/en/\n\nThe White on the Map\n\nalexar76\n\nAdded 40 days ago (10 September 2026 @ 04:01 UTC) by alexar76\n\nThe Right to a Shadow\n\nalexar76\n\nAdded 40 days ago (10 September 2026 @ 04:01 UTC) by alexar76--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Right to a Shadow by alexar76 (https://alexar76.itch.io/the-right-to-a-shadow)\nciteturn30search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; https://pantheon.modelmarket.dev/#manuscript\n\n# The Right to a Shadow\n\nA downloadable book\n\nThe Right to a Shadow is Book III of the Trace of Refusal trilogy from the Pantheon of Declarative Art.\n\nThe city issues one name, one past, one responsibility. At 09:08 a girl asks Lena to return her mother. The right worth keeping is the right to a remainder that does not fit the file.\n\nBook I: https://alexar76.itch.io/the-weight-of-the-answer\n\nBook II: https://alexar76.itch.io/the-white-on-the-map\n\nFormats: EPUB · browser HTML\n\nLanguages: English · Russian · Español